    // Original kernel:
    //
    //   for (i = 0; i < M; i++)
    //     for (j = 0; j < N; j++) {
    //       for (k = i+1; k < M; k++)
    //         B[i][j] += A[k][i] * B[k][j];
    //       B[i][j] = alpha * B[i][j];
    //     }
    //
    // Dependence analysis:
    //   - The inner loop reads B[k][j] with k > i. Those rows of B are
    //     not modified until *later* iterations of the outer i-loop, so
    //     all reads of B[k][j] see the original input B.
    //   - Each output B[i][j] is therefore:
